    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nHi there! I've been using this plugin for a long time, but recently I wanted to change the `add` mapping for visual mode and realized that it's not possible. It will be the same for normal and visual modes.\r\n\r\nFor example, I have really long mapping for surroundings, like `gsa`, `gsd` etc, but when I'm in visual mode, I wanna change it to just `s`, because `s` does the same thing as `c` by default in visual mode. So, binding it to `surround` will make it more valuable.\r\n\r\nI implemented this feature on my machine and seems to work fine, just small tweaks and that's it. I could open a PR if you don't mind and think that having such a thing is worth it :)",
    "closed_at": "2024-03-21T09:11:53Z",
