    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nThis was already discussed in #66. It resulted into documenting setup similar to 'tpope/vim-surround' which itself has the [way to customize `add` mapping in Visual mode](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/a822f42fd52952f03c7d98d50e8e56921444d699/doc/mini-surround.txt#L517-L519) (replace `'ys'` with `gsa` in your case).\r\n\r\nSo although there is precedent in 'mini.comment' to allow separate mappings for Normal and Visual mode, I think I don't really like this pattern as it adds extra complexity to the config structure without significant benefit (and in presence of a reasonable alternative solution).\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
