        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "damn, didn't even encounter that issue when searching for \"different mappings\"\r\nAnyway, I see your point, that workaround also works, but there's an additional step of deleting the mapping from visual mode that's applied from the config. Since I haven't used vim-surround, but started from mini.surround from the very beginning, I didn't even know there's such a thing in other plugins.\r\n\r\nThank you!",
